From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:04:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] irqchip/qcom-pdc: map qcom,pdc-ranges beyond the SPI range to
 ESPIs

qcom,pdc-ranges gives the GIC interrupt of each PDC pin as an SPI
number (INTID - 32), and qcom_pdc_alloc() always hands it to the GIC as
an SPI. On Glymur, whose last range <171 4104 36> lies past the SPIs,
the GIC still ends up on the right INTID but warns:

  GICv3: SPI 4115 out of range (use ESPI?)

Convert past the SPI range: INTIDs from 4096 are extended SPIs, so SPI
number n maps to ESPI n + 32 - 4096. On the HP OmniBook Ultra 14 this
puts the lid switch (PDC pin 182) on INTID 4147, as the ACPI tables
list it.

Based on a patch by Konrad Dybcio, whose offset of 4096 lands these
pins 32 extended SPIs too low.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20261102-topic-pdc_map_espi-v2-1-64431c8f8ac3@oss.qualcomm.com
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/irqchip/qcom-pdc.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/irqchip/qcom-pdc.c b/drivers/irqchip/qcom-pdc.c
index 82f146d7c1bc..ee8b5a9e3b1c 100644
--- a/drivers/irqchip/qcom-pdc.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/qcom-pdc.c
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 #include <linux/types.h>
 #include <linux/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/arm-gic.h>
 
 #define PDC_MAX_IRQS			256
 #define IRQ_ENABLE_BANK_MAX		BITS_TO_BYTES(PDC_MAX_IRQS)
@@ -597,8 +598,17 @@ static int qcom_pdc_alloc(struct irq_domain *domain, unsigned int virq,
 
 	parent_fwspec.fwnode      = domain->parent->fwnode;
 	parent_fwspec.param_count = 3;
-	parent_fwspec.param[0]    = 0;
-	parent_fwspec.param[1]    = pin_to_hwirq(region, hwirq);
+	/*
+	 * qcom,pdc-ranges numbers GIC interrupts as SPI numbers (INTID - 32),
+	 * also past the SPI range: INTID 4096 onwards are extended SPIs.
+	 */
+	if (pin_to_hwirq(region, hwirq) >= 4096 - 32) {
+		parent_fwspec.param[0] = GIC_ESPI;
+		parent_fwspec.param[1] = pin_to_hwirq(region, hwirq) + 32 - 4096;
+	} else {
+		parent_fwspec.param[0] = GIC_SPI;
+		parent_fwspec.param[1] = pin_to_hwirq(region, hwirq);
+	}
 	parent_fwspec.param[2]    = type;
 
 	return irq_domain_alloc_irqs_parent(domain, virq, nr_irqs, &parent_fwspec);
